# patch.plan — Cross-Plan Consistency Audit and Repair Plan

Status:
draft

Owner:
Human reviewer

Purpose:
Fix inconsistencies across Plans 8–16, governance files, ROADMAP.md, README.md, current_plan.md and next_plan.md discovered by cross-reference audit.

This patch is a planning and governance patch. It must not change implementation code, tests, backend code or corpus artefacts.

Priority:
Apply before activating Plan 8 for execution.

---

## 1. Audit basis

Reviewed files:

```text
README.md
ROADMAP.md
agent.md
history.md
current_plan.md
next_plan.md
plans/plan-8-groundtruth-validation.md
plans/plan-9-backend-smoke-readiness.md
plans/plan-10-connector-pageextractionir-validation.md
plans/plan-11-entity-proposal-document-validation.md
plans/plan-12-real-calibration-prior-generation.md
plans/plan-13-weighted-consensus-ir-real-outputs.md
plans/plan-14-linkedstructure-cross-page-semantic-linking.md
plans/plan-15-docling-export-validation.md
plans/plan-16-end-to-end-runner-mvp-corpus-evaluation.md
```

Main result:
The plan chain itself is mostly coherent from Plan 8 through Plan 16. Later plans, especially Plans 12–16, are cleaner. The biggest remaining issues are stale governance files, inconsistent run_log policy in earlier plans, ambiguous whitelist language in Plans 10–11, Plan 12 referencing a missing test, Plan 16 missing ROADMAP-required input classification, and README still documenting a removed CLI flag.

---

